# Every text file is stored with LF and checked out with LF, on every platform.
#
# This is not cosmetic here. Windows checkouts default to `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites
# line endings to CRLF in the working tree, and `biome check` reads the bytes it is given: on the
# Windows CI runner it reported 201 formatting errors, one per line, for files that are correct in
# the repository. A Windows developer hits the same wall locally, before ever pushing.
#
# `text=auto` normalizes on commit and leaves files git detects as binary alone, so the PNG, ICNS,
# and other binary assets under apps/desktop/src-tauri/icons and docs/assets are untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
